## Resolution: literal Find matching and execution contract

Accepted through the live Wayfinder discussion on 2026-10-26. The maintainer confirmed the [Unicode and execution choices](https://github.com/maksimgurenko/freelens-json-logs/issues/36#issuecomment-6428162884), the [lifetime, replacement and recovery choices](https://github.com/maksimgurenko/freelens-json-logs/issues/36#issuecomment-6428583227), and then answered “agree with all” to the 16,384-unit query limit, 100 ms pending feedback, 1,000 ms timeout and 4,096-range response limit. This comment consolidates the final contract; earlier partial agreements are its discussion history.

This resolves a technical planning decision. Production implementation remains outside this map. [Define Find state, reading anchors and occurrence identity](https://github.com/maksimgurenko/freelens-json-logs/issues/37#issuecomment-6408002921) remains authoritative, with its three-mode/regex references superseded by literal-only scope.

### Matching definition

- The query is exact, untrimmed literal text. Keep Match case and Whole words; omit the `.*` control and user regex syntax. An empty query clears Find results and decorations. Whitespace and punctuation in a nonempty query retain their meaning as characters.
- Search each retained record's **application text OR active extracted message**, excluding the Kubernetes transport timestamp. Return matching records in retained-window order and count each once, irrespective of the number of text matches or whether both sources match. Counts, navigation and scrollbar-record locations use this same complete list.
- Case-insensitive Find uses locale-independent Unicode simple/common folding. `K` matches `k`/`K`, and `σ` matches `ς`; `SS` does not match `ß`. Do not normalize, remove accents or apply locale tailoring. Match case uses exact character sequences. Obtain ranges from original source strings, never by treating indices in lowercased strings as original offsets.
- Whole words requires each adjacent original **code point** to be outside Unicode Letter (`L`), Number (`N`) and underscore, or absent at a string edge. Combining marks and other connector punctuation remain outside that agreed set. Do not substitute ASCII `\b`, locale segmentation or UTF-16-unit neighbor checks. In a native-regex implementation, scope case folding to the escaped query, keeping the boundary categories outside ignore-case semantics; U+0345 is a combining mark that folds to a letter and exposes the difference.
- Enumerate non-overlapping, left-to-right text matches independently in each source. `ana` in `banana` yields the first `ana`; the record counts once. Maintain that enumeration across requested display fragments; restarting at an arbitrary visible substring must not change which overlapping candidates win.
- Text-match ranges are nonempty half-open UTF-16 offsets into the identified original source, accompanied by record-occurrence reference and source provenance. Application-text and decoded-message offsets are independent. Never project a decoded offset into escaped JSON or infer a field path from offsets. Equal fallback-message/application strings may share scanning work only if both provenance meanings and offsets remain correct.

### Accepted bounds and feedback

| Item | Contract |
| --- | --- |
| Search scope | Existing retention: at most 1,000 records and 5 MiB original UTF-8 transport text. No retention/acquisition change. |
| Query | Maximum 16,384 UTF-16 code units. Validate before worker submission, including at the main boundary. Preserve oversized input, explain the limit and do not silently truncate or execute it. |
| Pending | Immediately mark new matching inputs pending and disable match navigation. Show `Searching…` after 100 ms if still pending; the delay applies to feedback, not to starting work. Start after committed edits without a typing debounce that changes query semantics. |
| Evaluation timeout | At 1,000 ms, invalidate the attempt, request actual execution cancellation and show local timeout feedback with explicit recovery. Include startup in the attempt; restarting or entering another stage must not reset its allowance. |
| Range output | At most 4,096 text-match ranges per reply. The measured four-uint32 representation occupies 65,536 bytes of offsets; protocol metadata is additional. Never allocate every dense match and trim afterward. |
| Exact matching | Preserve all matching records/provenance even when ranges are partial. A range cap never caps counts, navigation, active-result ordinals or scrollbar matching-record locations. |
| Ownership/concurrency | One reusable worker per active viewer that needs matching; at most one running evaluation and the newest replacement descriptor for that viewer. No backlog of older queries or navigation actions. |

Renderer feedback/expiration timers begin for the accepted logical attempt before dispatch. Main independently supervises execution before worker startup/posting and handles cancellation. Timeout invalidation prevents acceptance immediately even if actual exit is later. These are operating limits, not hard real-time guarantees: event-loop scheduling and native worker termination may be delayed. Record actual stop-to-exit time; a rejected Promise is not evidence that work stopped. Do not create a replacement worker until the previous one actually exits.

Distinguish ready zero matches, pending, oversized query, timeout and execution failure. Never show a previous input's count as a completed count for new input. Keep logs and query editing available. Failed/oversized/pending matching attempts do not become committed history entries; the existing valid-zero-hit history rule remains.

### Logical request/result interface

The spelling and wire encoding may change during implementation; these identities and meanings must remain:

```ts
type FindKey = {
  viewerEpoch: number;
  targetEpoch: number;
  instanceEpoch: number;
  windowRevision: number;
  messageRevision: number;
  queryRevision: number; // exact literal text + Match case + Whole words
};
type FindQuery = { text: string; matchCase: boolean; wholeWords: boolean };
type Source = 'application' | 'message';
// RecordRef is the shared, opaque, context-qualified occurrence reference.
type FindRecord = { ref: RecordRef; application: string; message?: string };
type RangeScope = { ref: RecordRef; source: Source; start: number; end: number };
type FindRequest = {
  requestId: number;
  key: FindKey;
  query: FindQuery;
  records: readonly FindRecord[];
  work: 'match' | 'ranges';
  rangeInterest?: { id: number; scopes: readonly RangeScope[] };
};
type MatchingRecord = { ref: RecordRef; application: boolean; message: boolean };
type TextRange = { ref: RecordRef; source: Source; start: number; end: number };
type FindReply =
  | { requestId: number; key: FindKey; kind: 'matches'; records: readonly MatchingRecord[] }
  | { requestId: number; key: FindKey; kind: 'ranges'; interestId: number;
      ranges: readonly TextRange[];
      coverage: readonly { scope: RangeScope; complete: boolean }[] }
  | { requestId: number; key: FindKey; kind: 'failed';
      reason: 'too-long' | 'timeout' | 'execution' };
```

- A match reply is the complete ordered matching-record list, not a sample of records with returned ranges. A range reply describes coverage explicitly; missing ranges never prove that a record/source does not match. Offset packing may use row ordinals within this immutable input only; resolve them back to its opaque references before acceptance, never to a later snapshot's numeric row indices.
- Range work can address currently visible source spans independently of exact matching. Preserve the whole-source matching definition when finding ranges that intersect a display span. Cap allocation/output, expose incomplete coverage, and do not automatically enumerate every range across the entire window. Geometry and source-to-presentation mapping belong to the rendering prototype.
- Exact matching takes precedence over decoration work. New query/window/message/context inputs invalidate old matching and ranges; new viewport interests replace old decoration interests without repeatedly starving still-current matching. A pending descriptor can retain only the latest logical inputs and display interest. Navigation need not wait for decoration after exact matching is ready.
- A separately requested range attempt that fails or times out does not invalidate already completed, still-current exact matching data. Preserve its counts/navigation and report incomplete highlighting with explicit recovery; do not label an undecorated hit as absent or block valid query-history commitment because decoration is pending.
- Accept a reply only while its full key, request ownership and relevant request/interest identity are current. Apply this to failures too. Valid matching data can update after Find dismissal, but cannot recreate a reading row, inspector, selection or reveal permission. Selection/reveal IDs and current occurrence lookup remain separate as specified in the state decision.
- Bound retained inputs to the current immutable window/message revision and newest replacement, with at most two logical sources per retained record. Clear replaced inputs, canceled output and owner-specific state at disposal. Source transfer/caching may be optimized without adding an unbounded window/query cache or changing provenance; the measurements do not require an optimization.

### Ownership, lifecycle and packaging

Use `node:worker_threads` owned by the main extension and extension-scoped SDK request/control/reply messaging. The main boundary binds an opaque viewer token to the actual requesting `webContents` **and sender frame/process-routing identity**. A token alone, cluster ID or shared `webContents` is insufficient. Reject foreign/disposed owners and malformed or out-of-bounds input before execution. Validate response identity and range bounds before use.

Create lazily for the first nonempty evaluation, reuse after successful work, and release on viewer inactivity/closure, target-owner disposal, owning-frame destruction, extension deactivation and app shutdown. Temporary inactivity preserves temporary Find state and surviving references. Recreate only when active and matching/range work is needed. Closing Find or entering Profiles can keep matching current while the viewer is active; neither restores a canceled jump. Empty input cancels its obsolete work and clears results; an already idle worker may remain reusable until the viewer becomes inactive or closes.

On supersession, invalidate immediately, stop obsolete executing work and retain only the latest replacement. Keep logical input revision separate from worker-generation identity so a late message from an earlier execution cannot affect a new worker. Disposal is idempotent and awaits actual exit; remove owner bindings, listeners and timers. Include cancellation/disposal during startup, before the ready message. If old execution has not exited, do not bypass that condition by spawning another worker. Preserve the proven actual-frame membership safeguard: the experiment's original `render-frame-deleted` listener failed, so it cannot be the sole assumed destruction signal. The production lifecycle verification must cover actual frame removal, same-frame replacement, inactive viewers and native window closure, including idle workers.

A timeout/loading/worker/matching failure stops that attempt and latches local feedback. Recover on an explicit query/mode edit or Retry action; snapshot refresh alone must not create a retry loop for that failed search. Retry recomputes current data without replaying an earlier selection/reveal intent. Do not silently switch execution mechanisms. An internal escaped-literal matcher error is an execution failure, never “invalid regular expression” blamed on the user.

Package a trusted, versioned worker program resolved relative to the installed main module, independently of host CWD. A versioned standalone build asset read by main and passed to `Worker(..., { eval: true })` follows the demonstrated actual-host loading pattern; extend the build/tarball allowlist to include that asset. Build it from the same pure matching implementation, without DOM, host globals or runtime package dependencies. User input is data, never worker program text. Native Unicode matching with fully escaped literal input, query-only case folding and the custom boundary rule is the implementation technique; do not accept a raw-pattern or arbitrary-flags branch. Update package/reproducibility checks to exercise the actual packed worker. No CSP, host preference or production host patch is required.

### Evidence and required regression coverage

The [immutable literal-only report](https://github.com/maksimgurenko/freelens-json-logs/blob/b3819c2f436ded65f9b2afa0631db9a7a5d9a25b/docs/research/find-literal-budgets.md) links its [raw samples](https://github.com/maksimgurenko/freelens-json-logs/blob/b3819c2f436ded65f9b2afa0631db9a7a5d9a25b/docs/research/find-literal-budgets/raw.json) and [reproducer](https://github.com/maksimgurenko/freelens-json-logs/blob/b3819c2f436ded65f9b2afa0631db9a7a5d9a25b/scripts/find-literal-budgets/measure.mjs). Evidence branch `research/find-literal-budgets` is pushed without a PR or merge. Its headless installed-Electron run records 416 measured outcomes: 368 correct completions and 48 internal matcher errors on 65,536-unit literals, with no deadlines. Every tested 16,384-unit case completes. Caller maximum is 12.11 ms; fresh startup maximum is 17.18 ms. The 4,096-range cases preserve exact counts with 65,536 offset bytes. All 16 fresh-worker recoveries pass; no owned worker remains.

The final semantic audit caught and corrected a candidate-worker discrepancy: global ignore-case made U+0345 count as a letter in a whole-word neighbor check. The [immutable original-neighbor addendum](https://github.com/maksimgurenko/freelens-json-logs/blob/a1524f4984334390b0602a2f12f9154878d2b5b7/docs/research/find-original-neighbors-addendum.md), [corrected raw samples](https://github.com/maksimgurenko/freelens-json-logs/blob/a1524f4984334390b0602a2f12f9154878d2b5b7/docs/research/find-literal-budgets/original-neighbors/raw.json) and [trusted-source derivation/reproducer](https://github.com/maksimgurenko/freelens-json-logs/blob/a1524f4984334390b0602a2f12f9154878d2b5b7/scripts/find-literal-budgets/measure.mjs) preserve both historical failing controls and the query-only-folding correction. All 21 earlier literal checks and 28 added regressions pass. The same 416-outcome matrix again has 368 completions, 48 internal 65,536-unit errors and no deadlines. All 64 tested 16,384-unit evaluations pass, maximum 10.45 ms; overall caller maximum is 14.00 ms. Startup maximum is 16.35 ms; all 16 fresh-worker recoveries pass and zero workers remain. The earlier report/raw remain historical evidence of the earlier candidate, not proof of this corrected boundary case.

The [actual Freelens loader/SDK ownership report](https://github.com/maksimgurenko/freelens-json-logs/blob/25bc0526100024c088bfd99911f6ebbb7330da0c/docs/research/find-main-host.md) establishes the host seam separately. Its final cluster Node JSON samples are approximately 15.0 ms median / 18.4 ms maximum, n=5. Do not add medians from different harnesses or equate CLI/IPC observations with rendered/native input performance. The corrected scoped-folding worker was checked headlessly, not newly installed in Freelens. The 100/1,000 ms values are accepted operating policies informed by these samples, not measured worst-case guarantees.

Implementation must cover:

1. All four literal modes; punctuation; empty/whitespace input; 16,384/16,385-unit boundaries; Unicode folding, normalization distinctions, astral offsets, supplementary word neighbors, marks/connectors and lone-surrogate behavior; U+0345 before/after a query with original-category boundaries; non-overlap across display fragments.
2. Actual retention boundaries, original-only/decoded-only hits, duplicate sources, exact count-once and 1,000-record order. Dense range truncation must preserve all records, provenance and late-window/visible-content access, with truthful incomplete-coverage feedback.
3. Every stale-key dimension, worker generation and range-interest replacement; stale successes and failures. Carry forward all occurrence/reading/inspection/IME/history/reveal traces from the state decision.
4. Pending feedback, timeout including startup, explicit Retry, failure latching, oversized input preservation, late exit and no overlapping replacement worker. Use controlled clocks/stalls for timer/state tests; tiny successful latency samples do not exercise the timeout branch.
5. Rapid typing/snapshot/profile replacement with bounded latest-only storage; matching priority over range work; no replay after manual scroll, Find dismissal, Profiles or inactivity. Keep following and Pause independent.
6. Actual packaged worker activation, foreign-frame rejection, frame destruction, inactive/closed viewers, disable/uninstall/shutdown and repeated cancellation/recovery. Verify real exit and bounded RAM/disk/thread/listener behavior over repeated lifecycles, rather than inferring a plateau from this short run.

Continue with [Validate text-safe highlights, hidden matches and scrollbar marks](https://github.com/maksimgurenko/freelens-json-logs/issues/38). It owns the live human rendering verdict, visible-range prioritization, incomplete-highlight presentation and DOM/geometry budget. Mounted UI responsiveness, attended native input and Windows/macOS remain explicit downstream acceptance gates. This resolution does not accept the pending production implementation or rendering prototype.
